      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two- patients had Melkersson-Rosenthal' syndrome. One of them had all the 3 components of the syndrome-facial paralysis, plicated tongue and macrocheilia, while the other had only 2 components-macrocheilia and plicated tongue. Oral antihistamine therapy for 3 weeks was ineffective in. both cases. But appreciable clinical response occurred after clofazimine therapy in both cases."},
